# homecloud-docs conventions

**Live site:** https://docs.web.holab.abrdns.com  
This repo auto-deploys on push to `main` (CI syncs to `so://docs/`).

## Product language

- **SO** not "storage" — URIs: `so://bucket/key` (never `s3://` in new docs)
- **MQ**, **MDB**, **Secrets** — use service short names consistently
- CLI examples: show PowerShell **and** bash when quoting/JSON differs
- Code blocks, commands, JSON: always **LTR**; keep `docs/he/` in sync for key user-facing pages

## What a page update should include

1. **What changed** — one-line summary
2. **Syntax / API** — exact commands or request shapes
3. **Examples** — copy-paste ready
4. **Breaking changes** — migration note if behavior changed
5. **CLI releases** — bump version note in `docs/en/cli/releases.md` (and HE) when tagging a release

## Before ship

```bash
mkdocs build --strict
```

## Do not

- Document only in a product README when the feature is user-facing (README can link here)
- Leave Hebrew key pages out of sync with EN
